To decompose the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we'll create a hierarchy of goals and tasks. The model will reflect the mission's requirements using AND/OR decompositions and specify runtime annotations for parallel, sequential, or fallback execution.

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                 | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Complete Resource Delivery | Ensure resources are collected and delivered to the requesting agent. | -                  | Perform   | -        |
| G2      | Execute Collection Phase   | Collect resources from specified storage locations.                  | #                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G3      | Execute Delivery Phase     | Deliver collected resources to the specified location.               | ;                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G4      | Manage Low Battery         | Handle low battery situations during collection and delivery phases. | FALLBACK(G4.1, G4.2) | Achieve   | G1       |
| G5      | Parallel Collection        | Assign multiple robots for parallel collection if needed.            | #                  | Perform   | G2       |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                   | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage          | Move to the storage location for resource collection.               | AND      | Storage           | 1                |
| AT2     | Request Resource             | Send a message to storage specifying the required resources.         | AND      | Storage           | 1                |
| AT3     | Wait for Resource Retrieval  | Wait until resources are retrieved from storage.                     | AND      | Storage           | 1                |
| AT4     | Deliver Resources            | Transport collected resources to the specified location.             | AND      | Delivery Location | 1                |
| AT5     | Return to Recharge           | Go back to the recharging station if battery is below 10% in collection. | AND      | Recharge Station  | 1                |
| AT6     | Return Resource to Checkpoint| Return resources to a checkpoint if battery is below 30% in delivery. | AND      | Checkpoint        | 1                |
| AT7     | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Assign the ongoing mission to another robot in case of low battery. | AND      | N/A               | 1                |
| AT8     | Trigger Alert                | Send an alert to the sector manager if resources cannot be returned to checkpoint. | AND      | N/A               | 1                |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2 [AND]**
- **G1 -> G3 [AND]**
- **G1 -> G4 [AND]**
- **G2 -> AT1 [AND]**
- **G2 -> AT2 [AND]**
- **G2 -> AT3 [AND]**
- **G2 -> G5 [AND]** (Parallel collection if multiple storages are involved)
- **G3 -> AT4 [AND]**
- **G4 -> G4.1 [OR]** (Low battery handling in collection phase)
- **G4 -> G4.2 [OR]** (Low battery handling in delivery phase)
- **G4.1 -> AT5 [AND]**
- **G4.1 -> AT7 [AND]**
- **G4.2 -> AT6 [AND]**
- **G4.2 -> AT7 [AND]**
- **G4.2 -> AT8 [FALLBACK(AT6, AT8)]** (Fallback if returning to checkpoint fails)

This model ensures that all aspects of the mission are covered, including resource collection, delivery, and handling low battery situations with appropriate fallback mechanisms.
